ities (government, UNHCR, joint).","source_id":"unhcr-asylum-applications-2026","series":[{"year":2006,"value":5}]},"asylum_decisions":{"note":"First-instance decisions, all authorities.","source_id":"unhcr-asylum-decisions-2026","series":[{"year":2007,"recognized":0,"complementary":0,"rejected":0,"closed":5,"total":5}]},"per_1000":{"year":2022,"value":0.0,"numerator":0,"denominator":623591,"sources":["unhcr-pop-2026","wb-pop-2026"],"note":"Refugees per 1,000 people living in The Republic of Montenegro."}},"headlines":{"over_time":{"text":"Refugees from Bosnia and Herzegovina in The Republic of Montenegro fell from {n0} (2006) to {n1} (2022)","nums":[5005,0],"years":[2006,2022]},"where_people_are":{"text":"The Republic of Montenegro hosts {p0} of all refugees from Bosnia and Herzegovina (2022), down from {p1} in 2006","pcts":[0.0,2.5],"years":[2022,2006]}},"steps":{"brief":true,"key_numbers":true,"over_time":true,"where_people_are":true,"inside_outside":true,"compare":false,"context":true,"other_angles":true,"limitations":true,"sources":true},"brief_sources":[],"footnotes":{"fn_1bb18f94":"2011 census figure adjusted to reflect number of persons that acquired naionality.","fn_2d8540ff":"In November 2017, jointly with the MoI and the MLSW, UNHCR carried out a field verification of all ex-Yugoslav refugees with unresolved status issues, including those at potential risk of statelessness. The field exercise covered 2,318 individuals (including 42% children) in 20 out of 23 municipalities. Based on the verification results, UNHCR reported on at least 145 persons at risk of statelessness and 460 in a statelessness like situation. During 2020 their number decreased to 118 and 349 respectively.","fn_4a83ed93":"In November 2017, jointly with the MoI and the MLSW, UNHCR carried out a field verification of all ex-Yugoslav refugees with unresolved status issues, including those at potential risk of statelessness. The field exercise covered 2,318 individuals (including 42 per cent children) in 20 out of 23 municipalities. Based on the verification results, UNHCR reported on at least 145 persons at risk of statelessness and 460 in a statelessness like situation.  During 2021 their number increased to 502 as 87 persons were identified as at risk of statelessness and, through a formal statelessness determination procedure introduced in 2018, 4 more persons were recognized as stateless by the Ministry of Interior of Montenegro.  Some 61 persons acquired nationality during the year.","fn_82e6f768":"In November 2017, UNHCR jointly with the Ministry of Interior (MoI) and the Ministry of Labour and Social Care carried out a field verification of all ex-Yugoslav refugees with unresolved status issues, including those of undetermined nationality. The field exercise covered 2,318 individuals (including 42% children) in 20 municipalities. The exercise identified 145 persons of undetermined nationality. Following the verification exercise, UNHCR and the MoI formed a working group to jointly assess each case and look for solutions in Montenegro or in the countries of origin.","fn_9a2036bb":"In November 2017, jointly with the MoI and the MLSW, UNHCR carried out a field verification of all ex-Yugoslav refugees with unresolved status issues, including those at potential risk of statelessness. The field exercise covered 2,318 individuals (including 42% children) in 20 out of 23 municipalities. Based on the verification results, UNHCR reported on at least 145 persons at risk of statelessness and 460 in a statelessness like situation.  During 2022 their number decreased for 46 persons, however new 47 persons at risk of statelessness were identified through a formal statelessness determination procedure introduced in 2018, leading to the total number of 494 persons at risk of statelessness at the end of 2022. By the end of 2022, 9 more persons were recognized as stateless by the Ministry of Interior of Montenegro. Some 46 persons acquired nationality during the year.","fn_a67531b5":"2011 census figure adjusted to reflect number of persons that acquired naionality.","fn_d4242bfe":"In November 2017, UNHCR jointly with the Ministry of Interior (MoI) and the Ministry of Labour and Social Care carried out a field verification of all ex-Yugoslav refugees with unresolved status issues, including those of undetermined nationality. The field exercise covered 2,318 individuals (including 42% children) in 20 municipalities. The exercise identified  145 persons of undetermined nationality. Following the verification exercise, UNHCR and the MoI formed a working group to jointly assess each case and look for solutions in Montenegro or in the countries of origin.","fn_da76e6b4":"2011 census figure adjusted to reflect number of persons that acquired naionality.","fn_f9ed21bc":"2011 census figure adjusted to reflect number of persons that acquired naionality."},"raw_files":{"conflict.csv":{"label":"IDMC GIDD, conflict and violence (HDX csv)","header":["iso3","country_name","year","new_displacement","new_displacement_rounded","total_displacement","total_displacement_rounded"]},"demographics/2021.zip":{"label":"UNHCR API download (demographics/2021.zip)","header":["Year","Country of origin","Country of origin (ISO)","Country of asylum","Country of asylum (ISO)","Population Type","Female 0 - 4","Female 5 - 11","Female 12 - 17","Female 18 - 59","Female 60","Female other","Female total","Male 0 - 4","Male 5 - 11","Male 12 - 17","Male 18 - 59","Male 60","Male other","Male total","Total"]},"persons_of_concern.csv":{"label":"UNHCR Refugee Data Finder download (persons_of_concern.csv)","header":["Year","Country of Asylum","Country of Origin","Country of Asylum ISO","Country of Origin ISO","Refugees","Asylum-seekers","IDPs","Other people in need of international protection","Stateless persons","Host community","Others of concern"]},"solutions/2006.zip":{"label":"UNHCR API download (solutions/2006.zip)","header":["Year","Country of origin","Country